Typical Instruments Used
*   Spirit-Reed Tenor Saxophone: A tenor saxophone modified with microtonal fingerings and equipped with bioluminescent valves, directly routed into bespoke real-time granular samplers and frequency-shifting neural networks.
*   Reverie Engines (Modular Synthesizers): Custom-built modular systems designed by the monastics, featuring unique modules named after specific dream states (e.g., "Lucid Lattice Oscillator," "Hypnagogic Drift Filter," "Archetypal Resonance Module").
*   Aether Percussion: Tactile transducers embedded in specialized performance floors or meditation benches, delivering sub-bass rhythms directly through the body, augmented by ceremonial gongs that trigger intricate arpeggiated synth sequences upon impact.
*   Vocal Encoders: Proprietary vocal processing units that transform chanted prayers, whispered subconscious narratives, or "glossolalia scripts" into complex, polyrhythmic synth lines and textural pads.

